        Root cause:
        The bug was primarily caused by improper reference counting of the `tcf_chain` objects, leading to potential use-after-free errors when chains were destroyed multiple times or when the reference count was not managed correctly. Specifically, chain 0 was treated as a special case, complicating the logic and increasing the risk of race conditions with RCU callbacks. The lack of a consistent reference counting mechanism made it difficult to ensure that chains were only freed when no longer in use.

